From e5c171935a4f6fee0444ed7560edb6c1f031991e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhael Skvortsov <mikhael.skvortsov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:50:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] board: samsung: exynos-mobile: Galaxy A40

Add the Samsung Galaxy A40 (SM-A405F, Exynos 7885) to the
exynos-mobile board, chain-loaded by S-Boot from the boot partition:

- clk and pinctrl drivers for the Exynos 7885 blocks U-Boot uses, and
  the device tree with its -u-boot.dtsi.
- USB gadget (fastboot, USB mass storage): an Exynos 7885 variant of
  the USB DRD PHY (its PMU isolation register, PHY_RST_SEL, the HS PHY
  tune value from the downstream kernel) with matching dwc3 fixes. The
  board code enables the USB PLL and FSYS clock gates, which S-Boot
  leaves off, and routes D+/D- through the S2MU106 MUIC to USB.
- dw_mmc: floor the data timeout at ~1 MB/s, since the controller clock
  cannot be raised and the nominal-rate timeout is too short for large
  transfers; the resulting set-rate failure is now debug output.
- Boot by sourcing /boot/boot.scr from userdata (partition 0x20) rather
  than sysboot/extlinux.conf, going straight to a bootmenu (boot,
  fastboot, USB storage, reboot, power off) with a short delay.
- CONFIG_CMD_BTRFS, so the root filesystem can be btrfs.
